            {
                "entry_id": "0eb0dd6d-283f-3b37-935a-e091b0dfb217",
                "word": "sandhi",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c9a36338-645b-42a9-82b6-6526384620af",
                        "entry_id": "0eb0dd6d-283f-3b37-935a-e091b0dfb217",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sandhis"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0e28ed63-039d-37ce-a88c-1e5f76320819",
                        "entry_id": "0eb0dd6d-283f-3b37-935a-e091b0dfb217",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Changement phonologique à la frontière des mots ou des morphèmes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac66791b-c8a0-4104-bf5c-05a5a772f4db",
                                "sense_id": "0e28ed63-039d-37ce-a88c-1e5f76320819",
                                "text": "Dans la prononciation, le français a conservé plus de traces du sandhi, ou de l’influence de quelques consonnes finales sur les mots qui les suivent; mais l’écriture n’a pas reproduit ces nuances de sons, qui ne sont sensibles qu’à l’oreille et ne sont rien pour les yeux."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aac3b0af-df69-427d-a182-cec9ad0f6151",
                        "source_entry_id": "0eb0dd6d-283f-3b37-935a-e091b0dfb217",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e28ed63-039d-37ce-a88c-1e5f76320819",
                        "target_lang_word": "Sandhi",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sandhi",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "233c7927-6818-3c4e-ac90-f692c731f203",
                                        "entry_id": "1f8e0a92-e076-3c89-a29e-e8a333cf44e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "lautliche Veränderung eines Anlauts unter dem Einfluss eines vorausgehenden Auslauts oder eines Auslauts unter Einfluss eines folgenden Anlauts im Wort oder zwischen Wörtern"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9129a4f1-10ae-482d-b2db-dfa70f0a485f",
                                                "sense_id": "233c7927-6818-3c4e-ac90-f692c731f203",
                                                "text": "„Einen Sonderfall bilden die Sandhis, die einen konsonantischen Wortanlaut verändern.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "917e6e7c-1daa-4a6a-9659-9d60994c9419",
                                                "sense_id": "233c7927-6818-3c4e-ac90-f692c731f203",
                                                "text": "„Eine nennenswerte allgemeine Theorie des Sandhi gibt es noch nicht, sondern nur mehr oder minder ausführliche Beschreibungen der Sandhi-Systeme einzelner Sprachen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d493e94-e6b2-43a9-809e-1b99e43dc0d0",
                                                "sense_id": "233c7927-6818-3c4e-ac90-f692c731f203",
                                                "text": "„Das Vorhandensein von »stillen« Halbbeats, also Disjunktur, verhindert, ihr Fehlen, also Junktur, ermöglicht den externen Sandhi (zwischen Wörtern) und die damit verbundenen segmentalen Erscheinungen wie Assimilation, Reduktion und Schwund von Konsonanten und Vokalen an syntaktischen Nahtstellen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f0b6fcb-0166-430b-a477-116ff1bfbc0b",
                        "source_entry_id": "0eb0dd6d-283f-3b37-935a-e091b0dfb217",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e28ed63-039d-37ce-a88c-1e5f76320819",
                        "target_lang_word": "sandhi",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sandhi",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2fbcede-337c-3198-a4fd-5f52f016322e",
                                        "entry_id": "0c846e6b-89db-34ad-b9d1-d79a88789954",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a wide variety of phonological processes that occur at morpheme or word boundaries, such as the fusion of sounds across word boundaries and the alteration of sounds due to neighboring sounds or due to the grammatical function of adjacent words."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81c10453-675c-4c4a-9811-86b753b27e60",
                                                "sense_id": "e2fbcede-337c-3198-a4fd-5f52f016322e",
                                                "text": "Mixed sandhi has two divisions, viz. when a word ending in a vowel is followed by a word beginning with a consonant, and when a word ending in a consonant is followed by a word beginning with a vowel. Cases of mixed sandhi are very few, and in the second division are limited to the changes of anusvâra before a vowel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82defb75-508d-4095-bc76-d077001f36d0",
                                                "sense_id": "e2fbcede-337c-3198-a4fd-5f52f016322e",
                                                "text": "The rules on sandhi in Pâli may be divided into rules on vowel-sandhi, and rules on mixed sandhi where a vowel and a consonant are concerned. Consonantal sandhi does not occur in Pâli."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
